# Gertruda, Mad Mary's daughter (docs/voice/gertruda.md; quest find_gertruda, village_of_barovia).
# start: the yellow guest room on the third floor. She joins as a guest when the party breaks the spell; Rahadin waits
# at the stairs (court_rahadin:intercept). returned: after the party gave her back.
# homecoming, mary_after, at_home: Mad Mary's house in the village (data/locations/mad_marys_house.json).

~ start
if flag.gertruda_met
Gertruda: You came back! I hoped you would. Nobody here talks, not properly. Rahadin only counts things.
-> menu
endif
set gertruda_met
Narrator: A girl of about sixteen sits on the edge of a curtained bed in a blue gown too fine for her, turning a ribbon over in her fingers. She jumps up when the door opens, and her face falls when she sees it isn't him.
Gertruda: Oh! You're guests too? Isn't it wonderful? I never saw a room this big. I never saw a room I wasn't locked into.
-> menu

~ menu
* Who are you? -> who
* Who brought you here? -> him
* [Insight DC 13] (Look at her carefully.) -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* [if flag.court_gertruda_insight] You're frightened, Gertruda. You have been since you got here. -> convinced_fear
* [if flag.gertruda_search_promised] Your mother isn't angry. She said the door is unlocked now. All three locks. -> convinced_mother
* [if flag.court_anastrasya_story] Anastrasya slept in this room once, in gowns like yours. -> convinced_anastrasya
* [if flag.court_ledger_read] The ledger downstairs has an account in your name. -> convinced_ledger
* [Cleric] (Say a blessing over her.) -> convinced_blessing
* [if not flag.court_gertruda_warned_him] [Persuasion DC 15] He doesn't love you. He collects. -> convinced_persuaded | persuade_fail
* We'll come back for you. -> END

~ who
Gertruda: Gertruda. From the village, the house with the shutters; maybe you passed it. My mother is careful. Very careful. I'd never been out at night before. I'd never been out.
if flag.mad_mary_met
Narrator: You know the house. You have heard the woman weeping in it.
endif
-> menu

~ him
Gertruda: He sang under my window. Old songs, the ones Mother never let me hear. Then a black carriage came with nobody driving it, and the door opened by itself, just like in the stories.
Gertruda: He says I'm to be a lady. He says soon.
interject tag:blunt: Soon. That's the word I don't like.
-> menu

~ insight_ok
set court_gertruda_insight
Narrator: Under the chatter her hands never stop on that ribbon, and she is humming, very quietly, without knowing she does it.
-> menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: She seems entirely, dazzlingly happy. Perhaps she is.
-> menu

~ convinced_fear
Gertruda: I'm not... I hum. Mother says I hum when I'm frightened. I've been humming since the carriage.
-> convinced

~ convinced_mother
Gertruda [afraid]: She said that? She isn't angry? All three locks. She'd never. She must have been so frightened.
approve kip_smudgewick +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You kept your word to Mad Mary and brought her message to Gertruda
-> convinced

~ convinced_anastrasya
Gertruda [afraid]: The lady downstairs, at the window? She was in this room? These were...
Narrator: She looks down at the blue dress as if it had moved.
-> convinced

~ convinced_ledger
Gertruda [afraid]: An account. In a book. Like a horse. Like buying a horse.
-> convinced

~ convinced_blessing
Narrator: A plain blessing, said plainly. Something in the room thins, like perfume when a window is opened, and the girl blinks as if waking.
Gertruda: Why did I... I don't even like blue.
inspire class:cleric: blessed the spell off a frightened girl
-> convinced

~ convinced_persuaded
Gertruda [sad]: He did say I was the prettiest one yet. Yet. I didn't think about that word.
-> convinced

~ persuade_fail
set court_gertruda_warned_him
Gertruda [angry]: You're jealous. Everyone is jealous of the girl in the story. I'm going to tell him what you said!
Narrator: She rings a little silver bell by the bed, and somewhere far off in the castle a door opens and closes.
-> menu

~ convinced
Gertruda [afraid]: I want to go home. I want to go home, and I don't know the way. It was dark in the carriage.
* Come home, Gertruda. Stay close to us. -> join
* Not yet. Wait here; we'll come back for you. -> wait

~ join
join gertruda
set gertruda_rescued
quest find_gertruda found
Gertruda: I'll be quiet. I'm good at quiet. I've had practice.
interject tag:cheerful: Stay behind me and you'll be fine. Mostly behind me. Generally in the direction of behind.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +3 kip_smudgewick +3 liriel_dawnsong +2 thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +1 ratatoille +1: You took Gertruda out of Strahd's guest rooms
-> END

~ wait
Gertruda: You'll come back? Yes. I'll wait. I'm good at waiting.
-> END

~ returned
Narrator: Gertruda sits on the bed in a new gown, a green one. She smiles at you politely, the way you smile at strangers.
Gertruda: He wasn't angry. He said I'd been frightened, and that it was natural. He said everyone is frightened before a wedding.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Home (Mad Mary's house, village of Barovia)

~ homecoming
leave gertruda
set gertruda_home
quest find_gertruda home
attitude mad_mary friendly
Narrator: Mary is on her feet before the door is fully open. For a moment neither of them moves. Then Gertruda says "Mother", very small, and Mary has her.
Mad Mary [sad]: You're cold. You're so cold. Where are your good shoes? Never mind. Never mind the shoes.
Gertruda: I'm sorry. I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
Mad Mary: Hush. The door's unlocked. It's staying unlocked. We'll learn how, the two of us.
Mad Mary: You brought her home. I said nobody listens. I was wrong, and I'm glad to be wrong. Sit. Let me mend something for you. Let me do something.
interject class:cleric: Bless this house, and its door, and the two of you in it.
-> END

~ mary_after
Mad Mary: She sleeps late now. I let her. I sit and listen to her breathing and I don't weep at all. The neighbours think I've gone madder.
-> END

~ at_home
Gertruda: Mother wants me to learn the woods. Just the edges, by day. I went as far as the well yesterday. It was wonderful. It was only a well.
-> END
